.TH SHDEPS 1 "2026-10-02" "shdeps" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shdeps \- declarative shell dependency manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shdeps
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shdeps
reads declarative config files and installs or updates shell tools via
system package managers, GitHub repos, GitHub release binaries,
Rust crates (\fBcargo install\fR), Go modules (\fBgo install\fR),
Python CLI tools (\fBuv tool install\fR), Node.js CLI packages
(\fBnpm install \-g\fR), or fully custom hooks.
Dependencies are declared in
.B *.conf
files within a config directory (default:
.IR \%${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:\-~/.config}/shdeps/ ).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B update
Install or update all configured dependencies. For supported shdeps installs,
also performs a quiet, best-effort self-update check before dependency updates.
.TP
.B self\-update
Update shdeps itself. Release installs update from the latest matching archive;
source checkouts use git pull --ff-only and skip dirty trees.
.TP
.B list
List all configured dependencies with columns for name, method, status,
and version details.
.TP
.BI check " name"
Check whether a specific dependency is installed.
Exits 0 if installed, 1 if not.
.TP
.BI dep-root " name"
Print the local root directory for a configured dependency when shdeps owns one.
.TP
.BI dep-path " name rel"
Print a path below a configured dependency root without requiring the final path
to exist.
.TP
.BI dep-file " name rel"
Print a path below a configured dependency root only when it is a readable
regular file.
.TP
.BI dep-links " name"
Print shdeps-owned public command links for a dependency as tab-separated
.IR command ,
.IR public-path ,
and
.I target-path
rows. The lookup is local and does not run hooks, package-manager probes,
network requests, or version commands.
.TP
.B health
Report problems with installed dependencies.
Reads only local config and state: no network, hooks, package-manager
queries, writes, or locks.
A healthy host prints nothing; otherwise each problem is one line of exactly
five tab-separated fields:
.IR severity ,
.IR package ,
.IR kind ,
.IR path ,
and
.IR detail .
.I severity
is
.B fail
or
.BR warn ;
.I package
and
.I path
are
.B \-
when not applicable; tabs and newlines inside a field become spaces.
Stable
.I kind
tokens:
.BR not-executable ,
.BR install-root-unmanaged ,
.BR blocked-transition ,
and
.B unreadable-state
(fail);
.BR missing-binlink ,
.BR dangling-binlink ,
.BR wrong-target ,
.BR dangling-link ,
.BR not-installed ,
.BR archive-backup ,
.BR deferred-post ,
.BR deferred-uninstall ,
.BR pending-post ,
.BR recovery-state ,
.BR stale-remote ,
and
.B temp-tree
(warn).
.B blocked-transition
marks an interrupted handoff that recovery refuses, so updates fail until it
is resolved.
Later releases may add kinds, never columns; ignore unknown kinds.
Exits 0 when healthy, 1 when problems are reported, and 3 when the report is
incomplete because some state could not be read or the report could not be
written.
.TP
.B prune
Remove orphaned dependencies that are no longer present in any config file,
or whose config entries are all excluded on this host by
.B os:
(or by a detected
.BR mgr: )
filters.
Accepts
.B \-y
to skip the confirmation prompt and
.B \-\-dry\-run
to preview what would be removed.
.TP
.B version
Print the shdeps version string.
.TP
.B help
Show the built-in help message.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIpath\fR
Config directory or file.
A path that is not an existing directory selects its parent directory.
Default:
.B $SHDEPS_CONF_DIR
or
.IR \%${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:\-~/.config}/shdeps/ .
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Bypass the TTL cache and check for updates immediately.
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-reinstall
Force reinstall all dependencies.
Implies
.BR \-\-force .
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress non-result output and interactive prompts.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output (log level 2).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help message.
.SS Prune options
.TP
.B \-y
Skip the confirmation prompt during prune.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be removed without actually removing anything.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Config files use a whitespace-delimited format.
All
.B *.conf
files in the config directory are loaded, sorted alphabetically.
Lines starting with
.B #
are comments.
.PP
.RS
.nf
# name            method           [cmd]            [aliases]                [filter]
jq                pkg
bat               pkg              apt:batcat
fd                pkg              apt:fdfind       apt:fd-find,dnf:fd-find
cgraf78/sley      github
cgraf78/ds        github:repo
neovim/neovim     github:release   nvim
ripgrep           cargo            rg
github.com/junegunn/fzf             go
ruff              uv
prettier          npm
dust              pkg              \-               \-                       os:macos
htop              pkg              \-               \-                       host:nas
nerd-fonts        custom
.fi
.RE
.SS Fields
.TP
.B name
Required.
Identifier for the dependency.
For
.BR github ,
.BR github:repo ,
and
.B github:release
methods, this is the GitHub
.IB owner / repo
(e.g.,
.BR neovim/neovim ).
For
.BR go ,
this is the full module path (e.g.,
.BR github.com/junegunn/fzf ).
For
.BR cargo ,
this is the crate name.
For
.BR uv ,
this is the PyPI package name.
For
.BR npm ,
this is the npm package name.
.TP
.B method
Required.
One of
.BR pkg ", " github ", " github:repo ", " github:release ", " cargo ", " go ", " uv ", " npm ", or " custom .
.TP
.B cmd
Command name to check for.
Defaults to
.IR name .
Supports
.B mgr:name
qualifiers for platform-specific command names (e.g.,
.BR apt:batcat ).
Use
.B \-
to keep the default.
.TP
.B aliases
For
.BR pkg :
comma-separated per-manager package name overrides (e.g.,
.BR apt:fd-find,dnf:fd-find ).
Use
.B NONE
to skip a specific manager.
.TP
.B filter
Combined platform, hostname, and package-manager filter using
.B os:
,
.B host:
,
and
.B mgr:
prefixes.
Comma-separated (e.g.,
.BR os:linux,host:nas,mgr:apt ).
Prefix with
.B !
to exclude (e.g.,
.BR os:!wsl,mgr:!pacman ).
Termux exposes
.B mgr:android
even though its package operations use APT-compatible commands internally.
Values within one prefix are alternatives; different prefixes must all match.
A filter containing only package-manager exclusions matches an unknown manager.
Filtered declarations may share one dependency name; the last matching
declaration is selected before ordinary last-wins override handling.
.PP
Treat
.B name
as a stable manifest identity.
To rename a dependency while reusing its command, first remove the old
declaration, run
.BR "shdeps prune" ,
then add the replacement declaration.
Shdeps rejects a replacement that conflicts with a differently named manifest
row so the old command cannot be mistaken for proof that the new provider is
installed.
.SS Install Methods
.TP
.B pkg
Uses the detected system package manager (brew, apt, dnf, pacman, zypper, or apk).
Batches all pkg installs into one command; retries individually on failure.
On first adoption, and whenever the manager, package alias, or command changes,
Shdeps verifies package-manager ownership even if the command already exists.
A durable proof preserves the command-only fast path on later healthy updates.
.TP
.B github
Resolves to
.B github:release
when the latest stable release has a compatible asset for the current host and
command; first installations without a compatible asset fall back to
.BR github:repo .
An existing matching release manifest row retains its release provider even
when upstream assets or metadata are unavailable. Use explicit
.B github:repo
to request a provider change.
The manifest and
.B shdeps list
record only the resolved concrete method.
.TP
.B github:repo
Clones from GitHub (the
.B name
field is the
.IB owner / repo ).
Prefers a local dev clone in
.B $SHDEPS_GIT_DEV_DIR
if present; otherwise pulls existing clones or does a fresh shallow clone.
Clean local clones with an upstream are updated with
.BR "git pull --ff-only" .
If that pull fails, shdeps preserves the user-owned clone and reports a
non-fatal warning instead of presenting potentially stale code as current.
Resolve the clone's branch divergence or connectivity problem before retrying
the update.
Managed clones are refreshed with
.B git fetch
and
.BR "git merge \-\-ff\-only" ;
a failure is a non-fatal warning naming Git's cause, recorded as
.IB name .repo.pull-failure
in the state directory until a refresh succeeds.
A failed fetch is retried once over the other GitHub transport (HTTPS or SSH)
of the configured URL, and origin is kept on that transport only if the retry
succeeded.
.TP
.B github:release
Downloads a pre-built binary from GitHub Releases (the
.B name
field is the
.IB owner / repo ).
Handles
.BR .tar.gz ", " .tar.xz ", " .tar.bz2 ", " .zip ", " .gz ", " .bz2 ", " .zst ,
and raw binaries.
If the latest stable release has no compatible asset, an owned executable
that passes a version probe is kept with a non-fatal update-pending warning.
The next ordinary update rechecks; incomplete publication does not refresh
resolver or release freshness. Missing or unusable owned commands, first
installations, and explicit
.B \-\-reinstall
still fail without a compatible asset. Download and checksum failures remain
errors. Shdeps does not fall back to arbitrary older releases.
.TP
.B cargo
Installs Rust crates via
.BR "cargo install --locked --root $SHDEPS_INSTALL_DIR/<name> <crate>" .
The binary is symlinked into
.BR $SHDEPS_BIN_DIR .
Requires
.B cargo
on
.BR $PATH .
.TP
.B go
Installs Go modules via
.BR "GOBIN=$SHDEPS_INSTALL_DIR/<name>/bin go install <module>@latest" .
The
.B name
field is the full Go module path (e.g.,
.BR github.com/junegunn/fzf ).
Requires
.B go
on
.BR $PATH .
.TP
.B uv
Installs Python CLI tools via
.BR "uv tool install <pkg>"
into a per-dep venv at
.IB $SHDEPS_INSTALL_DIR / <name> /tools
with the binary at
.IB $SHDEPS_INSTALL_DIR / <name> /bin/ <cmd> .
Requires
.B uv
on
.BR $PATH .
.TP
.B npm
Installs Node.js CLI packages via
.BR "npm install \-g \-\-prefix $SHDEPS_INSTALL_DIR/<name> <pkg>" .
The binary is symlinked into
.BR $SHDEPS_BIN_DIR .
Requires
.B npm
on
.BR $PATH .
.TP
.B custom
Hook-only.
Requires
.B exists()
and
.B install()
functions in the hook file.
.PP
For
.BR cargo ,
.BR go ,
.BR uv ,
and
.BR npm ,
if the required tool is absent and no active
.B pkg
dependency has that tool as its command,
.B shdeps update
exits with status 1 before installing any dependency
(the TTL-gated shdeps self-update check may already have run).
.SH HOOKS
Hook files are sourced from
.IB $SHDEPS_HOOKS_DIR / name .sh
(default:
.IR <conf_dir>/hooks.d/ ).
For github:* deps, hooks go in
.IB $SHDEPS_HOOKS_DIR / owner / repo .sh .
They may define the following functions:
.TP
.BI exists( name )
Required for custom deps.
Return 0 if the dependency is installed.
.TP
.BI install( name )
Perform the installation.
.TP
.BI version( name )
Print a version string.
.TP
.BI post( name )
Post-install setup.
Runs after any method if the dependency changed.
A failed post is retried on the next update.
.TP
.BI uninstall( name )
Cleanup during
.BR "shdeps prune" .
For custom deps this is the only cleanup path.
For other methods it runs before built-in cleanup.
.SH EXTRAS LINKING
For
.B github:repo
and
.B github:release
installs, shdeps auto-discovers and symlinks man pages
and shell completions to user-local directories:
.PP
.RS
.nf
Man pages       ~/.local/share/man/man<N>/
Bash completions ~/.local/share/bash-completion/completions/
Zsh completions  ~/.local/share/zsh/site-functions/
Fish completions ~/.local/share/fish/vendor_completions.d/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Tracked per-dep in
.IR $SHDEPS_STATE_DIR/<name>.links .
.SH LUA API
shdeps ships a Lua module at
.I lua/shdeps.lua
inside the shdeps root.
Installer activation publishes that
.I lua/
tree through the stable
.B $SHDEPS_LUA_DIR
link (default:
.IR ~/.local/lib/shdeps ),
which points at the active source, developer, or release tree.
The sibling
.I lua/shdeps/
modules are part of the same public release artifact.
.PP
The Lua module is a thin adapter over the shdeps CLI for runtime asset
resolution from Lua hosts such as Neovim and WezTerm. It does not parse shdeps
configuration itself.
.PP
.RS
.nf
local shdeps = dofile(os.getenv("HOME") .. "/.local/lib/shdeps/shdeps.lua")
local api = shdeps.new({ home = os.getenv("HOME") })
local setup = api.dep_file("cgraf78/termnav", "lib/termnav/nvim/setup.lua")
local env = api.env()
.fi
.RE
.PP
Lua hosts that start before shell init has normalized
.B PATH
can load
.I shdeps/bootstrap.lua
from the stable
.B $SHDEPS_LUA_DIR
tree:
.PP
.RS
.nf
local bootstrap = dofile(os.getenv("HOME") .. "/.local/lib/shdeps/shdeps/bootstrap.lua")
local shdeps = bootstrap.load({ home = os.getenv("HOME") })
local api = shdeps.new({ home = os.getenv("HOME") })
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B shdeps.new(options)
accepts
.BR home ,
.BR conf_dir ,
.BR bin ,
.BR bin_dir ,
.BR root ,
and
.B env
options.
The returned object exposes
.BR dep_root(name) ,
.BR dep_path(name,\ rel) ,
.BR dep_file(name,\ rel) ,
and
.BR env() .
Missing dependencies or unreadable files return nil.
.PP
.B env()
returns a fresh table with child-process environment overrides, including
.BR HOME ,
.BR SHDEPS_CONF_DIR ,
and a
.B PATH
prefixed with the selected shdeps binary directory when that binary is known by
absolute path.
.PP
.B bootstrap.load(options)
returns the located shdeps Lua API module.
.B bootstrap.new(options)
returns
.BR shdeps.new(options) .
.B bootstrap.paths(options)
returns the candidate
.I lua/shdeps.lua
paths in search order. Discovery checks explicit
.BR lua ,
.BR root ,
.BR lib ,
.BR git_dev_dir ,
and
.B home
options, the matching
.B SHDEPS_*
environment variables, and the bootstrap file's own root.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHDEPS_CONF_DIR
Config directory.
Default:
.IR \%${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:\-~/.config}/shdeps/ .
.TP
.B SHDEPS_HOOKS_DIR
Hooks directory.
Default:
.IR <conf_dir>/hooks.d .
.TP
.B SHDEPS_STATE_DIR
State and cache directory.
Default:
.IR \%${XDG_STATE_HOME:\-~/.local/state}/shdeps .
.TP
.B SHDEPS_FORCE
Set to
.B 1
to bypass TTL cache.
.TP
.B SHDEPS_BOOTSTRAP_FORCE
Set to
.B 1
to force provider freshness during
.B install.sh --bootstrap
without forcing the subsequent dependency update.
.TP
.B SHDEPS_REINSTALL
Set to
.B 1
to force reinstall all deps.
.TP
.B SHDEPS_QUIET
Set to
.B 1
to suppress non-result output and interactive prompts.
.TP
.B SHDEPS_REMOTE_TTL
Cache TTL in seconds.
Default: 3600.
.TP
.B SHDEPS_SELF_UPDATE_TTL
Self-update attempt TTL in seconds for
.BR "shdeps update" .
Default: 3600.
.TP
.B SHDEPS_GIT_DEV_DIR
Dev clone directory for github:repo deps (prefers <dir>/<repo> over fresh clone).
Default:
.IR ~/git .
.TP
.B SHDEPS_INSTALL_DIR
Base directory for github installs (uses <dir>/<owner>/<repo>).
Default:
.IR ~/.local/share .
.TP
.B SHDEPS_BIN_DIR
Directory for symlinks to installed binaries.
Default:
.IR ~/.local/bin .
.TP
.B SHDEPS_LUA_DIR
Installer-owned stable link to the active shdeps Lua API tree.
Default:
.IR ~/.local/lib/shdeps .
.TP
.B SHDEPS_LOG_LEVEL
Logging verbosity: 0=quiet, 1=normal, 2=verbose.
.TP
.B SHDEPS_JOBS
Maximum concurrent jobs for read-only probes and parallel non-package installs
.RB ( github* ", " cargo ", " go ", " uv ", " npm ).
Explicit positive values win;
.B 1
runs sequentially.
Default: host CPU parallelism (GitHub API reads cap the automatic value at 4).
.TP
.B SHDEPS_STATE_LOCK_TIMEOUT_SECS
Maximum seconds a mutating command waits for another live
.B shdeps update
or
.B shdeps prune
state lock holder before failing with lock metadata.
Default: 1800.
.TP
.B SHDEPS_CHECKOUT_LOCK_TIMEOUT_SECS
Maximum seconds a
.B github:repo
mutation or prune waits for the shared installer/shdeps checkout lock.
Values must be nonnegative decimal integers of at most 9 digits.
Default: 1800.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (dependency not found, install failure, etc.).
For
.BR health :
problems were reported.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (unknown command or missing argument).
.TP
.B 3
.B health
report is incomplete: some config or state could not be read (an
.B unreadable-state
row is printed) or the report could not be written.
.TP
.BI 128+ N
Interrupted by signal
.I N
after owned subprocess cleanup.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I \%${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:\-~/.config}/shdeps/*.conf
Default config files.
.TP
.I \%${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:\-~/.config}/shdeps/hooks.d/*.sh
Default hook scripts.
.TP
.I $SHDEPS_STATE_DIR/manifest
Installed dependency manifest.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install or update all dependencies:
.PP
.RS
.B shdeps update
.RE
.PP
Force update, bypassing TTL cache:
.PP
.RS
.B shdeps \-\-force update
.RE
.PP
Use an alternate config directory:
.PP
.RS
.B shdeps \-c ~/.config/myapp/ update
.RE
.PP
List all dependencies and their status:
.PP
.RS
.B shdeps list
.RE
.PP
Check if a specific dependency is installed:
.PP
.RS
.B shdeps check jq
.RE
.PP
List public command links owned by a dependency:
.PP
.RS
.B shdeps dep\-links cgraf78/sley
.RE
.PP
Preview orphaned dependencies without removing:
.PP
.RS
.B shdeps prune \-\-dry\-run
.RE
.PP
Remove orphaned dependencies without confirmation:
.PP
.RS
.B shdeps prune \-y
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR brew (1),
.BR apt (8),
.BR dnf (8),
.BR gh (1)
